.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
.Dd November 8, 2026
.Dt MOOBFS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm moobfs
.Nd mount, query and inspect a MoobFS layer and its workspaces
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm info
.Op Fl -json
.Ar path
.Nm
.Cm query
.Op Fl -json
.Op Fl -ino
.Op Fl -order Ar name type Cm asc | desc
.Op Fl -limit Ar N
.Op Fl -page Ar N
.Ar directory
.Op Ar term ...
.Nm
.Cm check
.Op Ar moobfs-check-argument ...
.Nm
.Cm diagnose
.Op Fl -json
.Ar path
.Nm
.Cm mount
.Ar lower mountpoint
.Op Fl -domain-depth Ar N
.Op Fl -nolinks
.Op Fl -noindex
.Op Fl -index-budget Ar B
.Op Fl -unsupported
.Op Fl -allow-open-lower
.Nm
.Cm status
.Op Fl -json
.Op Ar mountpoint
.Nm
.Cm workspace create
.Ar mount ns
.Op Fl -agents Ar a,b
.Op Fl -create-users
.Op Fl -dry-run
.Op Fl -json
.Nm
.Cm workspace grant | revoke
.Ar mount ns user
.Cm rw | ro
.Nm
.Cm workspace list
.Ar mount
.Op Fl -count Ar name
.Op Fl -json
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
answers attribute queries from the MoobFS layer's index and reports the state of a mount.
It uses the existing ioctls and tools; it adds no kernel interface.
MoobFS is an experimental research project.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm info
finds the moobfs_layer mount that holds
.Ar path
and prints what GET_INFO reports on its root: lower filesystem, interface versions, whether the
index is on, the domain depth, the index budget and build work, the attribute limits, and for an
administrator the index counters.
.It Cm query
asks QUERY2 on a domain
.Ar directory
and follows the cursor until the answer is complete, printing one path per line, relative to
.Ar directory .
On the root of a mount without domains it asks the mount-wide QUERY, which has no cursor.
Without
.Fl -order
the results are sorted by inode number.
.It Cm check
runs
.Xr moobfs-check 1
with the remaining arguments.
.It Cm diagnose
reports, without changing anything, what bounds a query on
.Ar path
by the caller: whether it is a domain directory, the index settings, the memory cgroup of the
process and the smallest memory.max above it with how often it was reached, the descriptor
limit, test-only module parameters left set and, for root, the index's use of its budget and
the tracepoints.
Each finding is a warning or a note; the exit status is 2 when a warning was printed.
Run it as the user, in the session that queries.
.It Cm mount
mounts the layer over
.Ar lower
at
.Ar mountpoint
with
.Xr mount 2 ,
as root, after checking the running kernel against the installed supported-kernels list, that
.Ar lower
is not itself a layer, and that a directory above it keeps every user but root out.
.Fl -unsupported
and
.Fl -allow-open-lower
skip the first and the last check.
The domain depth is 2 unless
.Fl -domain-depth
says otherwise.
.It Cm status
prints whether the module is loaded, its version and srcversion, and
.Cm info
for
.Ar mountpoint
or for every layer mount.
.It Cm workspace create
makes, as root, the namespace
.Ar ns
on a mount whose domain depth is 2:
.Ar ns
owned by root and the group moob-ns, mode 0750; its area shared, mode 2770 with the default ACL
u::rwx,g::rwx,o::---; and one area per agent, owned by the agent, mode 0700.
It adds the agents to the group.
With
.Fl -create-users
it creates the group and the agents as system users without a login shell.
.Fl -dry-run
prints the steps and does nothing.
It refuses an existing
.Ar ns
and never deletes anything.
.It Cm workspace grant | revoke
gives or takes
.Ar user
write access to the shared area through the group
.Pq Cm rw ,
effective at the next login, or read access through named ACL entries on
.Ar ns ,
shared and the default ACL of shared
.Pq Cm ro .
.It Cm workspace list
prints the namespaces, their areas, owners, modes and ACLs and, with
.Fl -count ,
how many files of each area carry the typed attribute
.Ar name ,
counted by a query as the caller.
.El
.Pp
When a query fails with ENOMEM,
.Cm query
reads the caller's memory cgroups again and says whether the memory.max of one of them or the
index budget refused it.
.Pp
.Nm
reads the mount record from
.Pa /proc/self/mountinfo .
When a sandbox denies that read, it recognises the layer by
.Xr statfs 2 ,
.Cm query
still asks QUERY2, and
.Cm info
takes the highest directory above
.Ar path
on the same device as the mount root; the build work and idle options are then unknown.
See docs/tools.md.
.Pp
A
.Ar term
is four words,
.Dq name op type value ,
up to four terms joined by AND; op is one of
.Cm eq , lt , le , gt , ge , prefix
or
.Cm exists ,
whose type and value are given as
.Dq - .
An operator ending in
.Sq \&?
also matches files without the attribute.
Types are
.Cm string , int64 , double , bool
and
.Cm time .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -json
print one JSON object
.It Fl -ino
prefix each path with its inode number and a tab
.It Fl -order Ar name type Cm asc | desc
return the files whose
.Ar name
attribute has
.Ar type ,
ordered by its value and inode number; terms may then be empty
.It Fl -limit Ar N
stop after
.Ar N
results
.It Fl -page Ar N
results per call, 1 to 4096 (default 4096)
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /usr/share/moobfs/supported-kernels , Pa /usr/local/share/moobfs/supported-kernels
the kernel releases
.Cm mount
accepts, installed by the moobfs-tools package and by make install
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 a system call failed; 2
.Cm diagnose
printed a warning; 3 the mount-wide query had more results than it can
return; 64 usage; 65 invalid terms or a query the kernel refused; 69 no layer there, a directory
that is not a domain, or the index off, a kernel outside the supported list, or a mount whose
domain depth is not 2 for
.Cm workspace create ;
75 a temporary refusal (index budget, a memory cgroup limit,
build limits, a domain that kept changing); 77 permission denied, or a command that needs root
run by another user.
For
.Cm workspace
and
.Cm mount ,
65 also means an invalid name, a missing user or group, or a refused lower, and 1 an existing
namespace or a step that failed.
The message on standard error names the cause.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl $ moobfs info /srv/memory
.Dl $ moobfs query /srv/memory/alice kind eq string decision
.Dl $ moobfs query --order created time desc --limit 10 /srv/memory/alice
.Dl $ moobfs diagnose /srv/memory/alice
.Dl # moobfs mount /srv/moobfs/lower /srv/memory --nolinks
.Dl # moobfs workspace create /srv/memory proj --agents planner,coder --create-users
.Dl # moobfs workspace grant /srv/memory proj auditor ro
.Dl $ moobfs workspace list /srv/memory --count kind
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr getfacl 1 ,
.Xr gpasswd 1 ,
.Xr moobfs-attr 1 ,
.Xr moobfs-check 1 ,
.Xr moobfs-index 1
.Pp
docs/tools.md and docs/operations.md in the MoobFS repository,
.Lk https://github.com/studiomoob/llmoobfs
